Scope. This review covers the apparatus half of the canonical chapter theories/becoming/chapters/THE-THEORY-OF-BECOMING.md, lines 1329–1897. That is 305 KB of the file's 962 KB: §7 AI alignment (2.8 KB), §8 open programme (97 KB), §9 formal spine (148 KB), §10 glossary (55 KB) and §11 earlier chapters (2 KB). It also covers:
- Ren's OPENING.md (v6);
- the generated theories/becoming/README.md;
- the required method page NONDUAL-METHOD.md;
- three September AI syntheses of the earlier 生生不息论 corpus that still sit at the theory root.

What holds. The formal claims made here are sound where they cite.
- Every Lean name in §7–§10 resolves. §9's 32 names not in the core receipt are periphery names; §10's two misses are namespaces.
- All 391 links in §7–§11 resolve.
- All 27 declarations cited in OPENING exist.
- The latest core receipt (20261016T124157.989030Z) shows 137 spine modules, 7,214 theorems and 9,912 spine declaration audits, all with empty axiom reports. The only generated constants that use an axiom are 99 `injEq` lemmas (on `propext`). The core compiles from Lean's prelude alone.

What is wrong is staleness, incompleteness and shape.
- §9 still quotes the previous receipt (7,089 theorems, a 126-module core closure).
- §9 omits the six P130 modules that landed today. One of them is Becoming.Runs, 'the one root'; the chapter never mentions it.
- §9 has 18 stale theorem counts and two malformed rows.
- Three hand-kept module listings disagree: the chapter (130 rows), the package README (106 rows) and the Becoming.lean docstring (122 bullets).
- §8 reads more like a changelog than an open programme:
  - its "further proofs" list states 26 closed results against 8 open markers;
  - its review history stops at the 16th review;
  - its list of what stays Ren's omits five readings the body marks "pending Ren";
  - it never states how integrated the spine is. The connectivity measure counts 1,019 of 7,214 theorems as apart, and the two families still do not reach each other by definition.
- §11 lists G0-WARRANT.md as an active study, although that file says "It is an adopted axiom". §11 also points to a catalogue last dated 10-08.
- Chinese and English are not kept equal:
  - Chinese only: §8's status table, 92 of 149 §9 rows and 165 of 192 §10 meanings;
  - English only: OPENING.md and NONDUAL-METHOD.md.
- NONDUAL-METHOD.md still calls the whole a "generative unfolding", which Ren corrected (P36b).
- The work board still shows P118–P127 as "verified in scratch, handed to the integrator", and Part II as "awaits Ren", although all of these are settled.

Shape. One 962 KB file is bound, with its sha256, as the statement source of 104 records, so any edit anywhere puts all 104 out of date. The chapter also states the theory three times: "the theory stated in full" (70 KB), the body, and "Part I stated whole" (105 KB). A finished canonical text would be:
1. a short bilingual statement of at most 80 KB, at the existing path, with anchor stubs;
2. one file per part for §1–§6, each binding its own records;
3. a reference volume generated from data: the module catalogue (from the Becoming.lean docstrings and the receipt, replacing three tables), a bilingual glossary, the open programme (from the records and the board) and the review history;
4. the historical layer moved out of navigation: the 128 chapter files last changed on or before 10-10, the syntheses and chapters/verification.

