areas.summary:
This area is the research layer from before the Becoming spine. It holds nine dated studies from 4–6 October 2026. It also holds the 5 October specialist-review dossier at the top of 2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review (REVIEW.md, FOUNDATION.md, its near-identical ORIGINAL, OPTIMAL-FOUNDATION.md, final-synthesis/, optimal-foundation/, review-support/), the application-evidence folder foundation-assessment/, and four small evidence folders under root-foundation. In total that is about 630 tracked files and about 16 MB.

The studies record the phase of the theory called "generative existence" or "alignment as the reproduction of its conditions":
- renewal, selection and observability constraints (integrated-evolution, claims U01–U33);
- physical and stochastic shared-renewal models with a small Lean ledger (support-and-shared-generativity);
- how concern forms, widens and revises its scope (concern-theory, revisable-concern and its settlement);
- direction and formation hypotheses (direction-frontier);
- joint formation and the first unified chapter set (unified-theory);
- a reading edition of the causal-foundations study;
- an evidence memo on generative health;
- representational optimality, an integrated synthesis, and an honest physical/originality/measured assessment. That assessment found the broad principle already anticipated in prior work and a zero primary gain on measured data.
Almost all results are AI hand proofs with exact finite checks. The only Lean is in older separate packages (experiments/shared-renewal-capability/formal, experiments/market-generativity/formal), and no instance theorem connects either to the spine.

**Links to the rest of the repo.** No record has its canonical source here. Five market records bind foundation-assessment/MARKET-INTERNET-DEGENERATION.md by path and sha256, and those hashes are current. THE-THEORY-OF-BECOMING.md cites none of these studies. About 50 historical or evidence chapters, the generated reading catalogue, LEAN-INDEX and source-index do cite them. README, RESEARCH, MAP, TIMELINE and OPEN-QUESTIONS link none of the nine studies, and _process/research/README.md lists none of them. Apart from links in historical chapters, the layer is orphaned from current navigation.

**Condition.** The prose is consistently honest about scope ("not proof-assistant certification", "not empirical validation"). Links in live, non-frozen files are clean except 72 path:line memo links. The problems are structural:
- entry pages still claim "latest", "current", "primary" or "next";
- the 10-09 rename altered copies labelled frozen or byte-preserved, so they no longer match their manifests;
- the reconciliation verifier now fails (60 errors, all in its navigation part), although its byte-preservation part still verifies all 2,689 captured files;
- a 1.7 MB snapshot from a repository-wide wording revision is misfiled under generative-health;
- reading editions duplicate sources byte for byte;
- third-party publisher files sit outside sources/;
- unrun empirical protocols never reached the generated open-questions view.

**What the spine supersedes.** The general structural content is now Lean-checked at broader scope in the pure core: renewal needs supply, a continuing family is fed from beyond, and the coarsest faithful description makes sense (Generation, Continuation, Admission, Description, Distinguishing). No correspondence theorems link the old statements to these. The domain models (chemistry, concern games, institutions, markets) are not superseded; they are historical evidence at their own scope.

**Recommendation.**
1. Now: write a study index, add historical banners, and move the frozen or duplicate sets to history.
2. As a phase for Ren to approve: move the nine studies at the same depth to _process/history/<study>/, so that outbound ../../../ links still resolve.
3. For the moves, reuse the receipt and re-derivation pattern of _process/architecture/check_rename.py and the git-blob fallback in verify_preservation.py.

