Claims 41, 42 and 52 (lines 342, 343, 356) and the instruments section (lines 141–143) present several 2025 claims tagged [mechanism]:
- ẇ = λCw with solution e^{λCt}w(0);
- values asymptotically align with C's leading eigenvector;
- the initial growth rate equals the covariance row-sum;
- eigenvalue budgeting.
The correction ledger restricts or rejects each of these. Row 29 says the general ẇ=aCw form and leading-mode dominance hold only under restrictions. Row 30 says covariance does not supply nonnegative weights. Row 32 says scale must be restored. Row 35 says the budget exceeds one and is not decay. The ledger's counterexamples are Lean-checked in LegacyReconciliation.lean. Only a banner at the top of a 1,200-line file warns readers, so a reader who lands on §C sees the refuted claims uncorrected.

